## Reading rules

- Before opening any file over ~1,000 lines, check size and headings first
  (`wc -lc`, `rg '^#'`), then read only the relevant section.
- **Never read a data file whole.** No `cat`/full-file Read on `.csv`, `.tsv`,
  `.ndjson`, `.json`, `.xlsx`, or any file in a data directory. Use
  `scripts/peek.sh <file>`, or `wc -l`, `head -n 20`, or a query script.
- Prefer `rg` with a match cap over listing directories recursively.

## Writing rules

- README: current state, entry points, commands, blockers, canonical outputs.
  Hard ceiling 250 lines / 25 KB. Enforced by `scripts/check-doc-budgets.sh`.
- README contains **no dates** except a single "Last updated" line. Per-run
  chronology goes in dated files under `history/` or `logs/`, never appended
  to a living document.
- CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md: durable invariants only, 150 lines max.
- One concise current handoff; everything prior becomes immutable dated history.

